        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 10/08/2025 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination revealed prolonged expiration and diffuse wheezing. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia or acute heart failure. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He is discharged in stable condition and I would kindly ask you to continue inhaled maintenance therapy and arrange close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
